# PLAN2 RT — Exec uses host_run on a CAS path

File: openOODA/audit/plan2_rt.oot
Wave 0. Ship 2. Read only. Do not implement.
Do not patch `chs_rt`. Do not patch `oodac`.
Do not edit `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda`.

Logline: Exec can call existing `host_run.run_oodac_run` on the
CAS leaf file path. No new C spawn API is required.

Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-launch-exec`.
SysCap is the system capability token. CAS is the content-addressed
store under `.ooda_modules/cas/<sha>`. A CAS payload path is the
host file path of the pinned `.oo` leaf, not the sha string alone.

Beats:
  1. State the verdict.
  2. Show what `run_oodac_run` accepts.
  3. Show that launch already has that host path.
  4. Show the live spawn path. Name side effects. Name non-blockers.

## 1. Verdict

No blocker.

`run_oodac_run` can take a CAS payload path.
DE1 can call it after the gate returns ok.
Do not edit `cli/host_run.oo`.
Do not add a C spawn in `runtime/`.
Do not call `sys_spawn`.

Status: `run_oodac_run` is done. Launch `--exec` is residual.

