## 3. What `run_oodac_run` accepts

Type: `pub fn run_oodac_run(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, rargs: List[String])`.

It walks `rargs`. The first token that is not a flag and not `--`
is `path`. It refuses `--fuzz` and `--engine bc`.
It requires `path != ""` and `path_exists(fs, path)`.
It then calls `run_oodac` with `run` and that `path` only.

`path_exists` is `oo_path_exists` in `chs_rt_fs.c`.
It opens the path for read. Any host file that the process can
open will pass. There is no sha256 type. There is no `.oo` suffix
check. There is no CAS parser.

`ooda run FILE` already uses this function (`cli/main.oo`).
A list with one host path is enough:

  `rargs = list_push(list_new(), path);`
  `run_oodac_run(fs, sys, rargs);`

`cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo` already imports `host_run.oo`.
`run_ooda_pm_launch` already has `&FsCap` and `&SysCap`.
No new import. No new main token. No `host_run` edit.

## 4. What a CAS payload path is

Launch already builds a host file path after the lock walk:

  `cas = root + "/.ooda_modules/cas/" + sha`
  `leaf = launch_pay_name(...)`
  `path = cas + "/" + leaf`

`pm_put_cas` writes `root/.ooda_modules/cas/<sha>/<fname>`.
That is a normal file. Launch already slurps it and hashes it
before the gate. The same `path` is what `--exec` must pass.

Do not pass the sha string alone.
Do not pass the CAS directory `cas`.
`path_exists` can return true for a directory on this host.
`oodac run` then fails when it reads that directory.
Pass `cas + "/" + leaf` only.

`pm_launch.oo` does not need a change.
`pm_launch_gate` already returns `ok` or `err …`.
Call `run_oodac_run` only after `ok`.

## 5. Spawn path. No new C API

`run_oodac` builds one shell line:

  `OODA_SRC_ROOT=… OODA_COMPILER=… OODAC_BIN=… <oodac> run <path>`

It quotes each token with `sq`.
It starts the child with `sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", cmd)`.

Emit (`c_emit_lower.oo`): `sys_exec` accepts `&SysCap` or
`&ProcessCap`. It lowers to `oo_sys_exec`.
Runtime (`chs_rt_caps.c`): `oo_cap_require_process` accepts
the Process token or the Sys token. SysCap supersedes.

`oo_sys_exec` (`chs_rt_sys.c`) does `fork`, `execvp`, and
`waitpid`. It does not use `system(3)`.
The child keeps `OODA_` and `OO_` keys and sets
`PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`.
The child keeps the parent stdout and stderr.
`LAUNCH_EXEC_OK` from the payload will show.

`oodac` `run` then checks, builds `path.bin`, and
`sys_exec`s that binary. That is the same tree as `ooda run`.

`sys_spawn` exists in `chs_rt_libfloor.c`.
The CLI does not call it. Do not add it.
Do not add a new symbol in `chs_rt`.

Today `--exec` calls `sys_exec` on
`test -e <path>; exit 0`.
That is the same SysCap. The child is not the payload.
Replace that line. Do not add a second spawn API.

## 6. Side effects. Not CAS blockers

These facts do not block a CAS leaf path.
DE1 must still obey them. Do not edit `host_run.oo`.

### 6.1 `process_exit`

`run_oodac` ends the CLI with `process_exit(0)` or
`process_exit(1)`. `run_oodac_run` does not return.

Call it last.
Do not print `ooda launch: ok` after it.
Do not print `"ok":true` before it.
On `--json` plus `--exec`, skip the JSON object.
The child stream is the result.
Gate fail still uses `launch_die` and never calls run.

`sys_exec` treats any non-zero child as Err.
The CLI exit is 0 or 1. That matches `ooda run`.

### 6.2 Build files next to the leaf

`oodac run` writes `path.bin` and `path.bin.tmp.c` next to
the source. That is how `ooda run FILE` works.

HARN must delete those files after the smoke.
`launch_pay_name` returns the first name that does not start
with `ingest_`. A leaf `name.oo` sorts before `name.oo.bin`.
Keep one `.oo` leaf in the CAS dir.

### 6.3 Compiler find

`find_oodac` probes cwd paths, then two XDG paths.
It does not read `OODA_COMPILER`.
This is the same rule as `ooda run`.
HARN must start the CLI from a tree that has `oodac_bin`,
`bootstrap/seed/oodac`, or `oodac/oodac`.

### 6.4 Extra argv and suffix

`run_oodac_run` drops tokens after the path.
This ship does not need payload argv.

`run_oodac_run` does not refuse ELF, empty, or a directory
that `fopen` can open. PV2 must refuse those before the call.

## 7. What is not a blocker

  Raw sha256: launch already has the leaf file path.
  Gate strings: `ok` / `err yank` / `err sha256 mismatch` /
    `err caps` already work.
  `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`: it gates `write_file`, not `gcc` via `sh`.
  Public `hello.oo` with no `main`: HARN adds a new fixture.
  `cli/main.oo`: launch already dispatches. Do not edit it.
  Child reap: `waitpid` is live. No new reap API.
  Line count: `cmd_pm_launch.oo` is 121 lines. Room exists.

## 8. DE1 call

After the gate is `ok` and `--exec` is set:

  Delete `test -e`.
  Pass the leaf `path` in a one-item list.
  Call `run_oodac_run(fs, sys, rargs)`.
  Do not wrap the payload bytes in a new `sh -c`.
  Quote rules stay in `host_run`.

Without `--exec`, print the path only.
Do not call `run_oodac_run`.

